===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|telecommunications}} The line or lines connecting the [[output]] of a [[transmitter]] to its [[antenna]].
#* {{quote-book|title=Wireless Telegraphy and Telephony|author=L. B. Turner|passage=When the capacity at the top has been made so large compared with the effective capacity of the '''uplead''' that the current in the latter is sensibly uniform, the length of that current is sensibly the full height ''h'' of the '''uplead''', which is the greatest available height with the given masts.|year=1921}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Optical Fiber Sensor Technology: Devices and Technology|page=137|author=L.S. Grattan|year=1997|passage=Effectively, the downlead and '''uplead''' for an individual sensor in the simple array becomes the downlead and '''uplead''' for a ladder in the subarray.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=The Communications Miracle: The Telecommunication Pioneers from Morse to the Information Superhighway|author=John Bray|year=2003|passage=Imagine the feelings of a very young engineer when required to measure the impedance of this vast aerial system with a “tuned circuit substitution” measuring set which looked minute compared with the 12-ft-diameter aerial '''uplead''', which required a gang to move i  to the measuring set.}}

